> Probably some painfully obvious answers to this one, but
>
> what are some strategies for reducing your AC as a monk?  The best I
> can figure is
>
> +5 cloak
> +5 shirt
> +5 gloves
> +9 or more divine protection
>
> for an AC of about -17 (which isn't bad).  Am I missing anything
> obvious?  How about for the early game when enchanting armor is not an
> easy task?

+5 CoMR, +5 shirt, +5 GoDex, +7 elven helm, +5 jumping boots = -22 AC.

That's without divine protection, so even without wearing an elven
helm and lucking everything to +5 (rather than +4) you really
shouldn't have problems getting to the -20 or -25 you want for
ascension.

On top of that, wearing a shield is fine (small ones allow most
casting), and once you max luck then you can wear body armor without
any problems.

In the early game, be more fastidious about BUC-testing and trying on
all the pieces of armor laying around the dungeon, and use standard AC-
avoidance tactics (ranged combat, spam Elbereth, spells, pets, etc)


